  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Cut the tofu pieces in half. Thinly slice the onion. Crush or finely chop 1 garlic clove. Discard the tough stems from the kale and coarsely chop the leaves. Coarsely chop the peanuts. Drain and rinse the chickpeas.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/153528/photos/large/prep_ingredients-0e50be55f0de7f21bb0d5419a2525231.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm tofu: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium deep frypan over medium heat. Cook the tofu for 2 mins each side or until browned. Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/153529/photos/large/cook_tofu-c93c93889dbabec6d7e4ab337684c18a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Soften onion: Add 2 tsp vegetable oil to the pan. Cook the onion and garlic, stirring occasionally, for 3-4 mins until softened. Add 1 tbs Indian masala seasoning (see Make it yours) and 1 tbs tomato paste and cook, stirring, for 1 min.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/153530/photos/large/soften_onion-4bfb869bd46f22f644038c82537b94ab.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook curry: Add the chickpeas, tomatoes and 180ml (¾ cup) boiling water to the onion mixture. Bring to the boil over high heat, then reduce the heat to medium and cook for 10 mins or until slightly thickened. Add the kale leaves and tofu and cook, stirring, for 2 mins or until the kale is wilted. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/153531/photos/large/cook_curry-1f6c73319d685db7c60799ae69a8d9fe.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Taste, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the curry among bowls, scatter over the peanuts and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/153532/photos/large/serve_up-fa3da40eeb33755963bb3bb57e8a2a5b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: We've suggested this amount of Indian masala seasoning for flavour, but if you prefer less heat or have little ones, reduce the masala to taste.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/153533/photos/large/make_it_yours-40652c0505a46168e95443730ef09537.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
